Phase 7: True SMP & Multi-Core Scalability

Goal: Promote make test-smp from experimental single-threaded execution to genuine parallel execution across all CPU cores.
• 1. AP (Application Processor) Bootstrap (arch/x86/, src/memory.rs)
	• Parse the ACPI MADT table to enumerate Local APIC IDs for all secondary cores.
	• Place a 16-bit real-mode trampoline in low physical memory (< 1MB), broadcast INIT-SIPI-SIPI IPIs (Inter-Processor Interrupts), and transition each AP into 64-bit long mode with its own GDT, IDT, and TSS.
• 2. Per-CPU State & Run Queues (src/scheduler.rs, src/interrupts.rs)
	• Dedicate the GS segment base (IA32_GS_BASE MSR) to a per-CPU control block (CpuLocal) holding the current thread pointer, core ID, and IRQ nesting depth.
	• Replace global scheduler locks with per-core run queues and work-stealing, plus TLB shootdown IPIs when unmapping shared pages.
• 3. Fine-Grained Locking (src/memory.rs, src/fs.rs)
	• Split coarse kernel locks into spinlock/mutex primitives with lock-ordering assertions so two cores can simultaneously allocate frames, read disk cache blocks, and handle syscalls without deadlocking.
• Verification (Makefile)
